---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const repo = 'https://github.com/cascadia-systems-lab/cascadia-lab.github.io';
---

<Layout
  title="Lab Notes"
  description="Open experiments, benchmarks, and field methodology from Cascadia Mobile Research"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero-topo section bg-gradient-to-b from-dark-bg via-dark-surface to-dark-bg">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Lab Notes</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary">
          An open notebook of experiments, benchmarks, and field methodology. Everything we test
          gets written up as it completes — including what doesn't work — so clients can check the
          evidence behind the services.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Research Questions -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Current Questions</h2>

      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="card card-hover">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-blue">Capture Methods</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <li>• Photogrammetry vs. LiDAR SLAM: accuracy, cost, and fit by site type</li>
            <li>• What a sub-250g platform can and cannot deliver for mapping work</li>
            <li>• Repeatable capture planning for change detection</li>
            <li>• Ground control and error measurement on a small-operator budget</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card card-hover">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-cyan">Self-Hosted Processing</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <li>• Open-source photogrammetry pipelines on owned GPU hardware</li>
            <li>• Cost and turnaround vs. commercial cloud processing services</li>
            <li>• LiDAR SLAM processing and point cloud registration</li>
            <li>• Storage and compute sizing for reconstruction workloads</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card card-hover">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-green">Spatial Analysis</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <li>• Change detection from repeat capture</li>
            <li>• Terrain, viewshed, and corridor analysis methods</li>
            <li>• Accuracy reporting clients can actually interpret</li>
            <li>• Deriving decision-ready products from raw reconstructions</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Planned Experiments -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Experiments on the Bench</h2>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="mb-4 flex flex-col justify-between gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
            <div>
              <h3 class="mb-1 text-xl font-semibold">Photogrammetry vs. LiDAR SLAM Accuracy</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Experiment ID: EXP-001</p>
            </div>
            <span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center rounded-full bg-accent-blue/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-accent-blue">
              Planned
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="mb-4 text-text-secondary">
            Capture the same site with drone photogrammetry and handheld LiDAR SLAM, reconstruct
            both, and compare the results quantitatively: geometric accuracy, coverage, capture
            time, and processing cost. The practical question every client asks — which method for
            which job — answered with measurements instead of vendor claims.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Photogrammetry</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">LiDAR SLAM</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">CloudCompare</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Accuracy Analysis</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="mb-4 flex flex-col justify-between gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
            <div>
              <h3 class="mb-1 text-xl font-semibold">Self-Hosted Photogrammetry vs. Cloud Services</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Experiment ID: EXP-002</p>
            </div>
            <span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center rounded-full bg-accent-blue/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-accent-blue">
              Planned
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="mb-4 text-text-secondary">
            Benchmark an open-source photogrammetry pipeline on owned GPU hardware against
            commercial cloud processing: reconstruction quality, turnaround time, and cost per
            project. Also the evidence base for our data-sovereignty offering — processing client
            data without third-party clouds has to be demonstrably competitive, not just principled.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Open-Source Pipeline</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">GPU Processing</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Cost Analysis</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Benchmarking</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="mb-4 flex flex-col justify-between gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
            <div>
              <h3 class="mb-1 text-xl font-semibold">Corridor Mapping Sample Deliverable</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Experiment ID: EXP-003</p>
            </div>
            <span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center rounded-full bg-accent-blue/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-accent-blue">
              Planned
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="mb-4 text-text-secondary">
            Produce a complete corridor mapping package — orthomosaic, elevation model, and analysis
            report — for a public right-of-way segment, published end to end as a worked example.
            Both a portfolio piece for infrastructure clients and a documented methodology anyone
            can evaluate.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Corridor Mapping</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Orthomosaic</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Case Study</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Public Data</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="mb-4 flex flex-col justify-between gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
            <div>
              <h3 class="mb-1 text-xl font-semibold">Magnetometry Processing Pipeline</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Experiment ID: EXP-004</p>
            </div>
            <span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center rounded-full bg-accent-purple/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-accent-purple">
              In Development
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="mb-4 text-text-secondary">
            Groundwork for drone-based geophysical survey: data handling, filtering, and
            visualization for magnetometer surveys, developed against public geophysical datasets
            before hardware is fielded.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Magnetometry</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Signal Processing</span>
            <span class="rounded bg-dark-border px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono">Geophysics</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Experiment Methodology -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Methodology</h2>

      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-blue">Measurement Principles</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <li>• Benchmark on actual hardware and real sites, not idealized conditions</li>
            <li>• Run multiple iterations to account for variance</li>
            <li>• Document environmental conditions alongside results</li>
            <li>• Use workloads representative of real client projects</li>
            <li>• Isolate variables to measure specific impacts</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-cyan">Documentation Standards</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
            <li>• Record hypothesis, methodology, and results</li>
            <li>• Include hardware specs and software versions</li>
            <li>• Document failures and negative results</li>
            <li>• Share reproducible processing scripts</li>
            <li>• Link to raw data where licensing allows</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Publications & Findings -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Published Findings</h2>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-dark-border bg-dark-bg p-8 text-center">
        <h3 class="mb-4 text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">Nothing Published Yet</h3>
        <p class="mb-6 text-text-secondary">
          Write-ups will appear here as the experiments above are completed. We would rather show
          an empty shelf than an inflated one.
        </p>
        <a
          href={`${repo}/tree/main/docs/experiments`}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="btn btn-secondary"
        >
          View Experiment Documentation
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Experimental Standards -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Standards</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            Performance and accuracy claims are backed by measurements on physical hardware under
            realistic conditions. Vendor benchmarks and theoretical estimates are treated as
            hypotheses to validate, not established facts.
          </p>
          <p>
            Failed experiments receive the same documentation rigor as successful ones. Negative
            results prevent redundant work — ours and other people's.
          </p>
          <p>
            Reports include complete methodology, hardware configuration, and software versions,
            with reproducible code where possible, so findings can be independently checked.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Call to Action -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">Follow the Work</h2>
        <p class="mb-8 text-text-secondary">
          Experiment documentation and methodology live in the GitHub repository. New results are
          published as experiments complete.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:justify-center">
          <a
            href={`${repo}/tree/main/docs/experiments`}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="btn btn-primary"
          >
            Experiment Index
          </a>
          <a href="/documentation/" class="btn btn-secondary">
            All Documentation
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
